      "title": "A shell colon does nothing. Use it anyway",
      "url": "https://refp.se/articles/your-shell-and-the-magic-colon",
      "discuss_url": "https://lobste.rs/s/eidh3u",
      "score": 19,
      "comments": 5,
      "author": "refp",
      "published": "2026-07-25T11:33:00Z",
      "bullets": [
        "The POSIX shell colon (`:`) builtin returns exit code 0, serving as a zero-overhead no-op for clean control flow logic.",
        "Use `:` to safely perform parameter expansions with side effects, such as initializing default variables via `: \"${VAR:=default}\"`.",
        "Truncate files efficiently without external processes using `: > file.txt`, or drive infinite loops via concise `while :; do` syntax."
      ]
    },
